  + /// Scan a terminal `AgentEnd` message list for a fatal, non-retriable turn
  + /// outcome (#652).
  + ///
  + /// Pure (no I/O, no globals) so it can be driven from tests against a
  + /// hand-built `Vec<AgentMessage>` — the stream-json event loop itself needs a
  + /// live agent. Delegates the actual verdict to
  + /// [`fatal_error_from_stop`](crate::prompt_retry::fatal_error_from_stop), so
  + /// the piped/stream-json path and the interactive path share one rule.
  + ///
  + /// Returns the **last** fatal assistant message in the list (the turn's final
  + /// state wins), or `None` when no assistant message ended fatally.
  + fn fatal_error_in_messages(messages: &[AgentMessage]) -> Option<String> {
